# Change account: released NeurIPS 2026 paper (paper-repo 6e496ca) → ICLR 2027 extension

## Writing revision (no new results): what changed and why

Baseline: the released paper (main text pp. 1–9 as released). This revision changes the writing only. No experiment was run; no number, registered verdict or conclusion changed; `numbers.tex` regenerates unchanged from the same `results/`. Text that left the main text moved to an appendix (listed below); nothing was deleted from the paper except repeated text.

### Strategy
The released main text read as a compressed test log: about 140 numbers in 9 pages, every baseline inline, internal labels (rung 1b–4, v3/v4, A1, N2, B1′, A2′) undefined, the illustration of the mechanism and every verdict table in the appendix. The revision (1) orders the argument as problem → mechanism → theory → held-out linear tests → reach of the account → limits, (2) puts one scorecard of the main registered tests in the main text, pointing to the appendix tables for every criterion (new Table 1, a re-layout of existing results) so the prose can interpret instead of list, (3) brings the race illustration into the introduction, (4) replaces internal labels by descriptions, and (5) moves detail needed only to check one test to Appendices B, E and F.

