- Sec. 2: De Melo Costa et al. read the EMA rate as a time scale that does not change which modes escape (was: as a shift of μ); the static rule attributed to Arbel et al. with an optimal ridge predictor and to Ponce et al. for a trained predictor and scalar input (was: both with a ridge predictor); Jing et al. for the spectrum, Garrido et al. for the effective rank.
- Sec. 4: Tian et al.'s per-mode system "at α = 1"; Ponce et al. added to the static threshold; "without the stop-gradient every direction decays" cited to Tian et al. Theorem 2 and Halvagal et al., and the no-predictor case to Tian et al.'s identity-predictor note.
- Sec. 6.1: Xie et al. (Adam not rotation-invariant), Kunstner et al. and Sabanayagam et al. as the sign-descent picture of Adam, Xie & Li as the ℓ∞ box of converged AdamW (was "the KKT point").
- Sec. 7: Chen et al. as making collapsed sets of parameters attractive.
- App. D: Arbel et al. and Ponce et al. separated; Li et al. as greedy rank-by-rank learning; Bao on the sixth-order eigenmode dynamics of the cosine loss; Kunstner et al. on class frequency; De Melo Costa et al.'s advice on predictor initialisation quoted instead of paraphrased.
- Bibliography: Ponce et al. → ICLR 2026; Bisulco et al. → ICCV 2025; Bao → Neural Computation 37(11), 2025; header comment corrected to the 18 Oct 2026 cutoff.

